nodes.body:
Pushed a recast on latest `main` after the review that `LLM.generate` should not grow Whisper-only logic.

This PR no longer touches `vllm/entrypoints/llm.py`. `WhisperGenerationMixin.generate` wraps `super().generate()` (HF `WhisperGenerationMixin` / `WhisperForConditionalGeneration`). Generic `LLM` is unchanged. Callers that want gzip/logprob fallback construct `WhisperLLM` and pass the long-form kwargs — see the updated description.

@DarkLight1337 this is the same split as HuggingFace: fallback lives on the Whisper mixin, not on `GenerationMixin`. Happy to move the helper entirely into user/eval code if you still prefer that; the mixin is the in-tree analog of HF so Python `LLM` users (including lmms-eval) do not each reimplement the gzip ladder.

